# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml — Root AI manifest for ProgBlocks

## Purpose

This is the root AI-assistant manifest for **ProgBlocks**, a pre-alpha,
dependency-free web component (`<prog-block>`) for rich code blocks in
technical documentation and wikis. Conceived for
[BerryWiki](https://github.com/metadatastician/berrywiki) but built
standalone from the start.

Read this file first, then
`.machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml` (where things ARE now), then
`.machine_readable/descriptiles/ANCHOR.a2ml` (what wins when README.md and
the verified facts disagree), then `README.md`.

The single verified source of truth this whole manifest set was written
against is
`.superpowers/sdd/progblocks-foamy-puzzle/FACTS.md` — established by direct
code reading and live API queries, 2026-08-03..08-07. If anything in this
file or elsewhere in `.machine_readable/` ever seems to contradict FACTS.md,
FACTS.md wins.

## Where things live

- `src/prog-block.js` (247 lines) — the `<prog-block>` custom element, the
  whole component. `src/prog-block.css` (182 lines) — its Shadow-DOM
  stylesheet.
- `src/modules/exporter.js` — export block content to JSON/CSV/Nickel/TXT
  (works, but the "CSV" and "JSON" paths are not real serialisation — see
  FACTS.md defect #7).
- `src/modules/smart-paste.js` — paste detection (array/matrix/text).
  Works; no tuple support.
- `src/a2ml-parser.js` — **stub**. Tree-sitter path commented out;
  `A2MLState` class is dead code; the parse function is never called.
- `src/modules/view-manager.js` — **entirely dead code**. Never imported by
  anything, despite containing the only real linter/WebSocket code in the
  tree.
- `src/k9-validator.js` — `K9Validator` class + `defaultValidator`
  instance. `validateNickel()` and `executeJustTask()` are fakes that are
  never called; `defaultValidator.checkMust()` IS called but ignores its
  only parameter.
- `assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm` — **not WebAssembly**. A 118-byte ASCII
  placeholder reading "// Dummy WASM file placeholder".
- `index.html` — the demo page, two `<prog-block>` elements. Registers and
  renders (see Invariants below).
- `tests/` — two `node:test` files: `prog-block.test.js` (smart-paste
  parsing) and `registration.test.js` (asserts
  `customElements.get('prog-block')` is defined).
- `contracts.ncl`, `package.k9` — self-description manifests. Neither is
  consumed by anything in this tree; treat them as declared intent, not
  enforced contract.
- `progblocks.launcher.a2ml` — the launcher's source config, correct as
  written. `progblocks-launcher.sh` — **generated** from it and marked "do
  not edit"; the generator currently loses its `{repo-dir}` tokens and the
  resulting script cannot start the server. This is an upstream
  `launch-scaffolder` bug, not a defect in the source config.
- `.github/workflows/` — `ci.yml`, `codeql.yml`, `secret-scanner.yml`, all
  pinned through `actions.lock` (`gh actions-lock`); `uses:` lines
  correctly carry tag refs, the lockfile holds the resolved SHAs.
- `.machine_readable/` — `descriptiles/` (CLADE, ANCHOR, META, AGENTIC,
  ECOSYSTEM, NEUROSYM, PLAYBOOK, STATE) + `contractiles/`
  (Must/Trust/Intend/Adjust/Dust/Bust) + `rsr-profile.a2ml` (declared
  capabilities: `web-ui`, `library` — deliberately minimal).
- `.well-known/` — `ai.txt`, `humans.txt`, `security.txt`.
- `README.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `GOVERNANCE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`,
  `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `LICENSE` (MPL-2.0) — the human documentation set.
  **README.md is aspirational; FACTS.md is authoritative on what actually
  works.** Do not treat the feature list in README.md as verified.

## Invariants (read before editing)

- **Licence is MPL-2.0.** SPDX header (`# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0`)
  must be the **first line** of every `.a2ml` file. Do not swap in AGPL or
  another licence.
- **Never hand-edit `progblocks-launcher.sh`.** It is generated by
  `launch-scaffolder` from `progblocks.launcher.a2ml`. The generated script
  currently cannot start the server (empty `REPO_DIR`, a startup-command
  search that can never match a non-executable string like
  `"python3 -m http.server"`, and a hardcoded absolute icon path that
  doesn't exist). Fix the upstream generator or file the bug there; do not
  patch the `.sh` output by hand.
- **Never re-inline action SHAs that `.github/workflows/actions.lock`
  owns.** The lockfile is the pin (`gh actions-lock`); workflow `uses:`
  lines correctly carry tag refs. "Fixing" them back to inline SHAs breaks
  the lockfile model and has caused `startup_failure` elsewhere in the
  estate.
- **The component must actually register.**
  `customElements.get('prog-block')` must be truthy after
  `src/prog-block.js` loads — there is a test for this
  (`tests/registration.test.js`), and it passes: `src/prog-block.js` was
  fixed to import `{ defaultValidator }` from `k9-validator.js` instead of
  the non-existent `{ validateK9 }`, so the module graph finishes loading
  and `customElements.define('prog-block', ...)` runs. Re-verify with
  `npm test` before relying on this if the tree has moved since
  2026-08-07 — do not assume it stays fixed without checking.
- **Do not document features the code does not implement.** In particular:
  there is no code/preview toggle, no templating wizard, no working live
  linter (the rendered panel is the hardcoded string `'<i>Linter ready</i>'`),
  and split-view is wired to a `:host([split-view="…"])` selector the JS
  never reflects onto the host attribute. See
  `.machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml` and FACTS.md's "Feature
  reality" section before writing anything that reads as a capability
  claim.
- **Nothing has been released.** Version numbers disagree across files
  (`1.0.0` in `package.k9`/`contracts.ncl`, `0.1.0` in
  `progblocks.launcher.a2ml`/`progblocks-launcher.sh`, `0.3.0` in
  `package.json`). Treat this project as pre-alpha; do not cut a
  tag without resolving the drift first.
- **There is a known, unfixed XSS surface.** Variant content is read via
  `innerHTML` and re-injected as HTML with no escaping anywhere; variable
  values are interpolated unescaped into `value="${val}"`. Do not add new
  features that write untrusted content through the same unescaped path.
